        {
          "text": "YÜ Chi 余集 (T. 秋室, H. 蓉裳), Jan. 29, 1739–1823, man of letters, painter and calligrapher, was a native of Jên-ho (Hangchow). A hsiu-ts'ai of 1757, he became a chü-jên in 1762. When his father died in Kwangtung in 1763 he made a journey to that province to bring back the remains.",
